# Session 12 demo requests. Run them top to bottom in IntelliJ (or VS Code REST Client).
# The login requests save the tokens into variables ({{sara}}, {{refresh}}, {{admin}}).
# Demo accounts (V6 migration): admin@flairs.dev, sara@flairs.dev, omar@flairs.dev, password secret123

### 1. No token: 401 with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks

### 2. Wrong password: 401, and the same message as an unknown email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "sara@flairs.dev", "password": "wrong-password"}

### 3. Log in as Sara (USER)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "sara@flairs.dev", "password": "secret123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("sara", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refresh", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 4. Who am I?  Paste the accessToken into https://jwt.io to read its claims (never paste a real production token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 5. Sara sees only her projects
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 6. Omar's project: 404, not 403 (do not confirm that it exists)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/3
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 7. Admin area as a USER: 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 8. Create a project: the owner comes from the token, not from the body
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Security", "description": "Session 12"}

### 9. Sara's tasks only
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 10. Refresh: returns a NEW pair, the old refresh token is now revoked
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"}

> {% client.global.set("refresh2", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 11. Use the OLD refresh token again: 401, and ALL of Sara's refresh tokens are revoked (reuse detection)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"}

### 12. So the new one fails too: 401. Sara must log in again.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh2}}"}

### 13. Log in as the admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@flairs.dev", "password": "secret123"}

> {% client.global.set("admin", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 14. ADMIN can list users (no password hashes in the response)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 15. ADMIN sees every project, including Omar's
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 16. Register a new USER (email is stored lower case)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "Nour@Flairs.dev", "password": "longpass1", "displayName": "Nour"}

### 17. Password too short: 400 with the errors map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "x@flairs.dev", "password": "short", "displayName": "X"}

### 18. Log out: revokes the refresh token (log in as Sara again first, request 3)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"}

### 19. CORS pre-flight from the allowed front end: 200 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin
OPTIONS http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization, content-type

### 20. CORS pre-flight from another site: 403
OPTIONS http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Origin: http://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET
